WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.850
<v Maya>Welcome to part four, the last part on the first lecture.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:10.560
<v Maya>We have done the order of testing, blood pressure and the three body measurement tests, which gave us no body fat percentage.

3
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:16.780
<v Maya>Today we go hunting for the percentage, with the skinfold caliper, the BIA machine and the Bod Pod.

4
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.370
<v Dev>And at the end, a comparison of everything so far.

5
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.270
<v Maya>Yes.

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:27.420
<v Maya>And a reminder of the pattern for every test: objective, procedure, then advantages and disadvantages.

7
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.770
<v Maya>There is only one test in this category.

8
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.720
<v Maya>The skinfold test, using a skinfold caliper.

9
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.510
<v Maya>Dev, have you seen the compass used to draw circles in school?

10
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.440
<v Dev>Yes, two arms, a pointed end on each.

11
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.260
<v Maya>The caliper looks like that.

12
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:47.020
<v Maya>You pinch and hold the skin to make a skin fold, and the caliper measures the thickness of that fold.

13
00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:52.340
<v Maya>A pinch of skin and fat measures subcutaneous fat, not the deep internal fat.

14
00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.930
<v Maya>The principle is simple.

15
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.560
<v Maya>The higher the subcutaneous fat, the higher the body fat percentage.

16
00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.030
<v Dev>Where do you pinch?

17
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.880
<v Maya>Three sites for each sex.

18
00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.960
<v Maya>Women: the triceps fold, the suprailiac fold, and the mid thigh.

19
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:14.670
<v Maya>Supra means above and iliac refers to the iliac crest, so the suprailiac is the fold just above the iliac crest on the waistline.

20
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:22.080
<v Maya>Men: the chest, midway between the top of the armpit and the nipple, the abdomen, one inch from the belly button, and the mid thigh.

21
00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.080
<v Maya>Mid thigh is the one site common to both.

22
00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.850
<v Dev>Why is it useful?

23
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.810
<v Maya>Portable, it fits in a bag or jacket pocket.

24
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.540
<v Maya>Easy to use once you know the three sites.

25
00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.960
<v Maya>Time saving, only a few seconds.

26
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:40.600
<v Maya>Disadvantages: it measures only subcutaneous fat, so it can't be relied on alone.

27
00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.230
<v Maya>It has a high standard error of plus or minus three percent.

28
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.620
<v Maya>It is not suitable for the very obese or the very lean.

29
00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.970
<v Maya>And some people dislike being pinched.

30
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.920
<v Dev>Explain standard error.

31
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.630
<v Maya>Accuracy is compared with the gold standard.

32
00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:01.830
<v Maya>If the gold standard says twenty percent body fat, a caliper result could be anywhere from seventeen to twenty three percent.

33
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.870
<v Maya>Calipers cost from about three hundred to five thousand rupees.

34
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.470
<v Maya>Spending more doesn't remove the error, because accuracy comes from the type of test, not the price.

35
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.600
<v Dev>And why not the very lean or very obese?

36
00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.690
<v Maya>A very lean person may have so little fat that you can't pinch a fold.

37
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.510
<v Maya>A very obese person may have more fat than the caliper arms can open to.

38
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:29.580
<v Maya>One note for your course: the lecture doesn't name the reference, the slide says compared with underwater weighing.

39
00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:33.150
<v Maya>And the E-book has slightly different abdomen and chest sites.

40
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.220
<v Maya>Follow the lecture and slides.

41
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:41.400
<v Maya>So, recap: skinfold gives a percentage, only subcutaneous fat, plus or minus three percent.

42
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.920
<v Maya>Next, the machine in most gyms that looks like a weighing scale with handles.

43
00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.200
<v Maya>People call it the BMI machine.

44
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.260
<v Maya>That's wrong.

45
00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.780
<v Maya>The correct name is BIA, Bioelectrical Impedance Analysis.

46
00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:59.800
<v Maya>Bio is life, electric is electric current, impedance is resistance, analysis is study.

47
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.930
<v Dev>So it measures how much a current is resisted.

48
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.820
<v Maya>Yes.

49
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:11.800
<v Maya>You stand barefoot on metal plates, which are electrodes, and a very mild current enters your body, felt as at most a mild vibration.

50
00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.230
<v Maya>The machine measures how much difficulty the current faces.

51
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.930
<v Maya>The scientific principle is that water is a good conductor of electricity.

52
00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.300
<v Dev>And what does that have to do with fat?

53
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:31.770
<v Maya>A muscle cell is seventy five percent water, plus twenty percent protein, four percent intramuscular triglyceride and one percent glycogen.

54
00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:36.220
<v Maya>A fat cell is only ten percent water and ninety percent triglyceride.

55
00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.180
<v Maya>So a muscular person has more water, and the current passes smoothly.

56
00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.590
<v Maya>A person with more fat has less water per cell, so the current is restricted.

57
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.960
<v Maya>From the resistance, the machine reports fat and muscle.

58
00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.300
<v Dev>So it sees visceral fat too?

59
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:55.680
<v Maya>Yes, it considers both visceral and subcutaneous fat, and gives a percentage.

60
00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.840
<v Maya>That's better than the earlier tests.

61
00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.450
<v Dev>Types of machine?

62
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:04.790
<v Maya>Foot to foot looks like a weighing scale, analyses the lower body, and estimates the whole body.

63
00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:09.570
<v Maya>Hand to hand looks like a game controller, analyses the upper body, and estimates.

64
00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.570
<v Maya>Hand to foot, the latest, has electrodes in hands and feet, so there's no estimation.

65
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.510
<v Maya>Prices run from about ten thousand rupees to forty five lakh.

66
00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:27.100
<v Maya>High end ones give segmental analysis for arms, chest, abdomen, thighs and pelvis, and also intracellular and extracellular water.

67
00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.030
<v Dev>What happens in the test?

68
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:39.660
<v Maya>Step on barefoot, the machine weighs you, the height is entered manually after you've measured it with the stadiometer, you hold the hand electrodes with thumbs on the metal at chest level, arms still.

69
00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.530
<v Maya>It gives body fat percentage, muscle mass and BMI.

70
00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.460
<v Dev>What are the prerequisites?

71
00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.710
<v Maya>The goal is neutral hydration.

72
00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:48.900
<v Maya>Well rested.

73
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:54.700
<v Maya>Empty stomach, no food, no water, and no coffee, even black, because coffee comes with water.

74
00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.500
<v Maya>No alcohol, with a gap of forty eight hours.

75
00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.940
<v Maya>No exercise, with a gap of twelve hours, because sweating dehydrates you.

76
00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:07.460
<v Maya>No metal objects, like jewellery, watches, phones and belts, because metal conducts.

77
00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:11.190
<v Maya>And women should not test during periods, because of fluid loss.

78
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.980
<v Dev>How long since food?

79
00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:17.770
<v Maya>Do it first thing in the morning, so there's automatically at least about six hours since dinner.

80
00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:23.930
<v Maya>The E-book says no eating or drinking for four hours, also emptying the bladder and avoiding diuretics.

81
00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.430
<v Maya>If in doubt, follow the stricter rule.

82
00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.170
<v Dev>Pros and cons?

83
00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:34.190
<v Maya>Advantages: hardly a minute, easy enough that even front desk staff can run it, and it only needs a socket.

84
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:41.120
<v Maya>Disadvantages: some models show standard error, so it's not as accurate as the gold standard, though better than the earlier tests.

85
00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:47.680
<v Maya>And hydration changes the result, so a more hydrated person will show more muscle, which can't be relied on.

86
00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.290
<v Dev>So pause and think.

87
00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:53.810
<v Dev>Why does drinking water before a BIA test make the reading wrong?

88
00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.030
<v Maya>You tell me.

89
00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.780
<v Dev>Water conducts, so the machine counts the extra water as more lean mass.

90
00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.710
<v Maya>Right.

91
00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.670
<v Maya>Recap.

92
00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:09.480
<v Maya>BIA passes a mild current, water conducts, muscle is seventy five percent water and fat ten, and hydration is the weakness.

93
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.010
<v Maya>Last machine today.

94
00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.490
<v Maya>Bod is body, pod is a sealed chamber.

95
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.250
<v Maya>It's a big egg shaped chamber.

96
00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:23.920
<v Maya>It's also called the air displacement method, and it belongs to the densitometry methods, which use body density to find body fat percentage.

97
00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.490
<v Dev>Body density?

98
00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.320
<v Maya>Body density equals body mass divided by body volume.

99
00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:40.340
<v Maya>The machine then applies the Siri equation, body fat percentage equals four point nine five divided by body density, minus four point five zero, all times one hundred.

100
00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:42.090
<v Maya>You don't need to memorise it.

101
00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.050
<v Maya>The computer does everything.

102
00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.880
<v Dev>How does it get volume?

103
00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.300
<v Maya>Air displacement.

104
00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:52.580
<v Maya>The seat is in the test chamber, with a reference chamber behind it holding the scale for body weight.

105
00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.790
<v Maya>A diaphragm measures air volume.

106
00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.890
<v Maya>First it measures the volume of air in the empty chamber and stores it.

107
00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:02.540
<v Maya>The person sits in, displacing some air, and it measures again.

108
00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.770
<v Maya>The difference between the two is the volume of the person.

109
00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.660
<v Maya>Body mass comes from the scale, so density, then body fat.

110
00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.400
<v Dev>Doesn't opening the door change things?

111
00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:17.100
<v Maya>The machine analyses air volume and pressure and compares with the stored values.

112
00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:22.320
<v Maya>The person also breathes out into a tube, so it measures the air in the lungs and removes it.

113
00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.070
<v Maya>That improves accuracy.

114
00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:31.680
<v Maya>And the person wears a swimsuit or spandex, and a tight swimming cap, because clothes carry air and hair has gaps that hold air.

115
00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.550
<v Dev>Example of results?

116
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:41.340
<v Maya>In the video, total weight was ninety seven kilograms: eighty two kilograms of fat free mass and fifteen kilograms of fat mass.

117
00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.400
<v Maya>Fat free mass is the same as lean body mass.

118
00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:48.900
<v Maya>Fifteen divided by ninety seven is about fifteen point five percent.

119
00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:53.360
<v Maya>That percentage was calculated for the notes, the recording did not state it.

120
00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.950
<v Dev>Advantages and disadvantages?

121
00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.340
<v Maya>Accurate, comparable to the gold standard, though not the gold standard itself.

122
00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.550
<v Maya>Time saving.

123
00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.740
<v Maya>No technical expertise needed.

124
00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:12.140
<v Maya>Suitable for all ages, patients, obese people, children, the very elderly and hydrophobic people, meaning those afraid of water.

125
00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:16.990
<v Maya>Disadvantages: expensive, and not available in India, as written on the board.

126
00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.690
<v Dev>Hydrophobic?

127
00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.050
<v Maya>The next test, in part five, puts the person underwater.

128
00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:26.090
<v Maya>Someone afraid of water can't manage that, but can sit in the Bod Pod.

129
00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.270
<v Maya>Quick recap.

130
00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.410
<v Maya>Bod Pod is air displacement, density, then Siri.

131
00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.380
<v Maya>Compare.

132
00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:37.320
<v Maya>Waist circumference, waist to hip ratio and BMI: no percentage, risk or category only.

133
00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:41.890
<v Maya>Skinfold: percentage, subcutaneous only, plus or minus three.

134
00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:47.130
<v Maya>BIA: percentage, visceral and subcutaneous, hydration sensitive.

135
00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:51.440
<v Maya>Bod Pod: percentage, accurate, but expensive and hard to find.

136
00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.780
<v Dev>And when we choose the best test, accuracy isn't the only factor.

137
00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.950
<v Maya>Right, affordability and availability matter too.

138
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.150
<v Maya>That is where part five picks up.

139
00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.090
<v Dev>Five things to remember?

140
00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:08.700
<v Maya>One, skinfold measures subcutaneous fat with a plus or minus three percent error.

141
00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:14.540
<v Maya>Two, BIA works because water conducts, and muscle is seventy five percent water, fat ten.

142
00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:21.820
<v Maya>Three, BIA needs an empty stomach, no exercise for twelve hours, no alcohol for forty eight hours, no metal.

143
00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:27.430
<v Maya>Four, Bod Pod finds volume by air displacement, then density, then the Siri equation.

144
00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:33.310
<v Maya>Five, Bod Pod is accurate and suits everyone, but is expensive and not available in India.

145
00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.470
<v Dev>Next, lecture two, with underwater weighing and DEXA.

146
00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.770
<v Maya>See you in part five.

